<%#
  Owner-only editing affordances, Instagram-style: the controls live on the
  thing they change rather than in a panel above the page.

    - hover the cover or the avatar -> a drop zone appears over it. Click to
      pick a file, or drag one on. Either way it uploads and the page comes
      back with the new photo.
    - every other region gets a quiet "Manage" button that leads to the real
      editor for that kind of thing, because a collection or a paid post has
      far more fields than belong in an overlay.

  Each drop zone is a real multipart form wrapping a real file input, so with
  JS off it is still a working "choose a file, press the button" upload. JS
  adds drag-and-drop and submit-on-choose.
%>

<%# The one persistent marker that you are looking at your own page. Kept to
    a single line: the point of this design is that the page looks like the
    page, not like an admin screen. %>
<div class="ie-strip">
  <div class="ie-strip-inner">
    <span class="ie-strip-label">
      <span class="ie-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      Your page. Hover a photo to replace it.
    </span>
    <%= link_to "Open dashboard", dashboard_path, class: "ie-mini" %>
  </div>
</div>
